         "Food delivery riders, who number about 10 million across China, are not about to disappear. Drones only cover set routes. In the Futian business district, riders still carry many meals the last 200 metres from a landing station to the lobby.",
         "Labour researchers said riders worried about the long-term effect on jobs, but that for now drones handled only a small share of deliveries. Shenzhen authorities plan to open more than 1,000 drone landing points across the city by 2027, part of what officials call the low-altitude economy.",
